language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Handshaking at a dinner: Hilary and Jocelyn plus num_couples invited couples; nobody shakes hands with themselves or their spouse, and Jocelyn asks everyone but herself how many hands they shook, getting all different answers.
given num_couples : int(1..)
$ people 1 and 2 are Hilary and Jocelyn; couple k is people 2k-1 and 2k
find shakes : matrix indexed by [int(1..2*num_couples+2), int(1..2*num_couples+2)] of bool
$ hands[i] is the number of hands person i has shaken
find hands : matrix indexed by [int(1..2*num_couples+2)] of int(0..2*num_couples)
find hil : int(0..2*num_couples)

branching on [shakes]
such that
$ nobody shakes hands with him or herself
forAll i : int(1..2*num_couples+2) . (shakes[i,i] = false),
$ nobody shakes hands with his or her spouse (Hilary and Jocelyn are a married couple too)
forAll k : int(1..num_couples+1) . (shakes[2*k-1,2*k] = false),
$ a handshake is between two people, so it is the same whichever way it is read
forAll i : int(1..2*num_couples+2) . forAll j : int(1..2*num_couples+2) . (shakes[i,j] = shakes[j,i]),
$ the number of hands each person has shaken is the number of handshakes that person takes part in
forAll i : int(1..2*num_couples+2) . (hands[i] = (sum j : int(1..2*num_couples+2) . toInt(shakes[i,j]))),
$ couples other than Hilary and Jocelyn are interchangeable: within a couple the first person has fewer hands, and couples are ordered by that first person's count
forAll k : int(2..num_couples+1) . (hands[2*k-1] < hands[2*k]),
forAll k : int(2..num_couples) . (hands[2*k-1] < hands[2*k+1]),
$ Jocelyn asks everyone except herself, and all the answers are different
allDiff([hands[i] | i : int(1..2*num_couples+2), i != 2]),
$ Hilary's answer is the number of hands she has shaken
hil = hands[1]
